# Package documentation

## Documentation language

All project documentation — `docs/**`, package `README.md` files, root `README.md`, `GLOSSARY.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` — is written in **English**.

- New documents: English only.
- When editing an existing document written in another language, translate the **whole file** to English in the same change — no half-translated files.
- Historical records (`docs/plans/*`, `docs/adr/*`) stay as written unless edited.
- Code comments are not documentation — this rule does not apply to them.

## Where it lives

- Index: [README.md](../../README.md) (root) — overview, build, links only.
- Layer architecture: [docs/architecture.md](../../docs/architecture.md).
- **Client (Godot):** [docs/client-protocol/README.md](../../docs/client-protocol/README.md), LLM index: [docs/llms.txt](../../docs/llms.txt).
- **Package:** `README.md` in the package directory, e.g. `internal/usecase/room/README.md`.
- Wire state layout: [docs/wire-state-codec.md](../../docs/wire-state-codec.md) (codec).

## Rule for agents and developers

When a package's **behavior, contract, or public API** changes — update that package's `README.md` in the **same PR/task** (plus the related wire-doc when applicable).

Who writes and when: see [.cursor/rules/ai-companion.mdc](ai-companion.mdc) (trust zones). This rule defines **what** to update; the companion defines **whether it may be edited now**. If zoning blocks the edit (code still red-zone, codec changes not yet approved) — ask for permission or wait for the user's code fix, then write the docs **as-built**. Before a large batch of docs, ask what exactly to document — no over-engineering for hypothetical futures. Wire/client-protocol docs after confirmed codec changes — the agent writes them itself.

Do not duplicate long tables in the root README — link to the package instead.

